et executed as scripts.'=>'The nosniff value prevents browsers from guessing file types. Stops MIME-confusion attacks where text files get executed as scripts.','What does X-Content-Type-Options do?'=>'What does X-Content-Type-Options do?','Controls browser APIs: camera, microphone, geolocation, payment, USB. Setting them to () disables access, preventing malicious scripts from using sensitive device features.'=>'Controls browser APIs: camera, microphone, geolocation, payment, USB. Setting them to () disables access, preventing malicious scripts from using sensitive device features.','What does Permissions-Policy do?'=>'What does Permissions-Policy do?','Controls iframe embedding. SAMEORIGIN allows only your domain to frame your pages. Prevents clickjacking attacks where malicious sites embed your site in hidden iframes.'=>'Controls iframe embedding. SAMEORIGIN allows only your domain to frame your pages. Prevents clickjacking attacks where malicious sites embed your site in hidden iframes.','What does X-Frame-Options do?'=>'What does X-Frame-Options do?','Your server sends the CSP with Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only instead of Content-Security-Policy. The browser checks the policy but blocks nothing — only reports violations. Perfect for testing.'=>'Your server sends the CSP with Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only instead of Content-Security-Policy. The browser checks the policy but blocks nothing — only reports violations. Perfect for testing.','What is Report-Only mode?'=>'What is Report-Only mode?','WordPress sites load resources from many sources: theme, plugins, Google Fonts, analytics, CDNs. CSP must list every legitimate source. Miss one and something breaks.'=>'WordPress sites load resources from many sources: theme, plugins, Google Fonts, analytics, CDNs. CSP must list every legitimate source. Miss one and something breaks.','Why is CSP hard to configure?'=>'Why is CSP hard to configure?','Content Security Policy tells browsers which resources can load on your page. Anything not listed is blocked. It is the strongest protection against XSS attacks.'=>'Content Security Policy tells browsers which resources can load on your page. Anything not listed is blocked. It is the strongest protection against XSS attacks.','What is CSP?'=>'What is CSP?','Disable HSTS in plugin settings. Clear browser cache: Chrome chrome://net-internals/#hsts → search domain → Delete. If on preload list, submit removal at hstspreload.org (takes months).'=>'Disable HSTS in plugin settings. Clear browser cache: Chrome chrome://net-internals/#hsts → search domain → Delete. If on preload list, submit removal at hstspreload.org (takes months).','How do I undo HSTS?'=>'How do I undo HSTS?','Only if your entire domain (including all subdomains) works over HTTPS. Preload is hardcoded in browsers and difficult to undo. Removal takes months. Test thoroughly first.'=>'Only if your entire domain (including all subdomains) works over HTTPS. Preload is hardcoded in browsers and difficult to undo. Removal takes months. Test thoroughly first.','Should I enable HSTS Preload?'=>'Should I enable HSTS Preload?','Minimum for preload: 31536000 (1 year). Recommended: 63072000 (2 years). Start with 86400 (1 day) to test, then increase.'=>'Minimum for preload: 31536000 (1 year). Recommended: 63072000 (2 years). Start with 86400 (1 day) to test, then increase.','What max-age should I use?'=>'What max-age should I use?','HTTP Strict Transport Security tells browsers to always use HTTPS. Even if someone types http://, the browser upgrades to https:// automatically. Prevents protocol downgrade attacks.'=>'HTTP Strict Transport Security tells browsers to always use HTTPS. Even if someone types http://, the browser upgrades to https:// automatically. Prevents protocol downgrade attacks.','What is HSTS?'=>'What is HSTS?','Can it conflict with other security plugins?'=>'Can it conflict with other security plugins?','WordPress 4.7 and above. Uses only WordPress core APIs with no external dependencies.'=>'WordPress 4.7 and above. Uses only WordPress core APIs with no external dependencies.','What WordPress version is required?'=>'What WordPress version is required?','Yes. Cloudflare passes through headers set by WordPress. Some headers like HSTS can also be set in Cloudflare dashboard — avoid setting them in both places to prevent duplicates.'=>'Yes. Cloudflare passes through headers set by WordPress. Some headers like HSTS can also be set in Cloudflare dashboard — avoid setting them in both places to prevent duplicates.','Does it work with Cloudflare?'=>'Does it work with Cloudflare?','Does it work with caching plugins?'=>'Does it work with caching plugins?','Does it work with Nginx, LiteSpeed, or IIS?'=>'Does it work with Nginx, LiteSpeed, or IIS?','Yes. Every security header, every configuration option, every protection this plugin offers today will remain completely free. No features will ever be moved behind a paywall. Shield is a separate set of brand-new tools built on top. Revenue from Shield funds free updates for all users.'=>'Yes. Every security header, every configuration option, every protection this plugin offers today will remain completely free. No features will ever be moved behind a paywall. Shield is a separate set of brand-new tools built on top. Revenue from Shield funds free updates for all users.','Is the free version really free forever?'=>'Is the free version really free forever?','Will this plugin slow down my site?'=>'Will this plugin slow down my site?','Adds HTTP security headers to your WordPress site: HSTS, CSP, Permissions Policy, X-Frame-Options, and more. These headers tell browsers how to protect visitors from attacks like XSS, clickjacking, and protocol downgrades.'=>'Adds HTTP security headers to your WordPress site: HSTS, CSP, Permissions Policy, X-Frame-Options, and more. These headers tell browsers how to protect visitors from attacks like XSS, clickjacking, and protocol downgrades.','What does 